# Agentic / implementation routing

Do not infer current project status from historical phase documents, Git history, model memory or tool-specific configuration.

Start from:

- `IMPLEMENTATION.md` — repository implementation/agentic entry point;
- `knowledge/index.md` — portable OKF v0.2 progressive-disclosure entry;
- `docs/agentic_development_foundation/README.md` — live ADF execution status;
- `docs/agentic_development_foundation/authority_scope_policy.md` — shared human-directed action/authority policy;
- root `AGENTS.md` — shared repository constitution;
- `.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` — canonical portable workflow when a named DMTZ workflow is relevant;
- `docs/implementation/README.md` — sole living implementation-program status authority;
- `docs/implementation/agent_reference_index.md` — secondary stable-ID/canonical-document bridge;
- the active ADF or implementation group plan;
- `docs/concepts/phase_010/09_architecture_consolidation_validation_exit/implementation_handoff.md` — frozen architecture handoff.

**ADF-A through ADF-D are complete. ADF-E is the next required Agentic Development Foundation group.** Implementation 001 follows the complete Agentic Development Foundation exit.

Tool/workflow rules:

- Cursor uses root `AGENTS.md` plus scoped `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`;
- Cursor consumes DMTZ workflows natively from `.agents/skills/`;
- Claude Code uses `.claude/CLAUDE.md` plus thin `.claude/commands/` bridges to the same `.agents/skills/` source;
- Codex uses root `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/skills/` natively;
- `tool_compatibility.json` records documented compatibility; ADF-G owns runtime smoke evidence;
- no adapter/skill may create a parallel semantic/status authority.

Human-directed action classes:

- A1 review/inspect/plan: do not edit unless changes are also requested;
- A2 change/build/fix: perform in-scope edits and directly necessary support/validation without repetitive permission prompts;
- A3 external/destructive/scope-expanding: require explicit task-specific human authorization plus repository/team gates;
- A4 architecture/semantic change: follow DMTZ change control.

Workflow boundary:

- selecting or auto-matching a skill inside the current human task does not create new work;
- `implement-group` stops at the selected task/group;
- `review-change` remains read-only unless fixes are separately requested;
- `run-conformance` does not rewrite requirements to make checks pass;
- `update-traceability` requires actual supporting evidence;
- `exit-review` cannot self-waive unresolved mandatory gates.

Knowledge rules:

- use `knowledge/index.md` for first-hop routing when location is not already known;
- traverse one category/concept at a time;
- follow canonical `resource` links for exact meaning;
- treat OKF metadata as knowledge-artifact metadata only;
- canonical resources win over OKF summaries.

Other rules:

- read only the active group and domain references needed for the task;
- search exact stable IDs instead of loading whole phases;
- ADF work may add agent configuration, knowledge/workflow routing and deterministic validation helpers;
- product code remains under the active implementation package, not implied by ADF work;
- do not create unrelated follow-on work, delegate implementation to other agents, or merge/deploy unattended;
- completing the requested group authorizes reporting the next step, not starting it;
- tool memory/preferences are noncanonical;
- implementation convenience never supersedes accepted contracts;
- design-scenario PASS is not executable implementation proof.
